es this means that  the admirals may not actually be here  but at the same time we have to assume  that this is an extremely strong fleet  after all the world government  dispatched this fleet to take down  whoever defeats kaido so they must be  prepared to take on an extremely strong  opponent on top of that they have been  ordered to take over all of wano their  mission is not just to step in and take  out the straw hats who have already been  weakened by the battle against kaido and  big mom no they are there to take direct  control of an entire kingdom for an  undisclosed period of time which is a  far more daunting task and which will  require the use of overwhelming force  this is a plot point that has to be  resolved before wano can properly  conclude and momo's statement that he is  not ready to open up the borders of wano  just yet hints at the fact that a  confrontation with this fleet is coming  now we know that luffy zorro and the  other heavy hitters on the straw hat  side are in no shape to engage in  another brutal fight at least not yet so  this showdown with the world government  fleet could play out in a few different  ways the first option is that the straw  hats will just escape wano before the  world government fleet can capture them  which would give luffy zoro sanji and  everyone else enough time to recover  from the kaido fight but that would be a  very anti-climactic ending to the wanos  story because the people of wanos still  wouldn't be free the superhuman effort  that everyone put into defeating kaido  and the beasts pirates will have been  all for nothing because the tyrannical  rule of kaido and orochi would just be  replaced by the tyrannical rule of the  world government the people of wano  would still be oppressed their dreams of  freedom would be shattered and the  entire arc would feel like a pretty big  letdown especially from the perspective  of wano's inhabitants oda has really  focused in on the struggle of wanos  people and on their dreams of freedom  many times over the course of this arc  so i don't see him just leaving them in  the hands of the world government as the  straw hats flee for their lives so what  else could potentially happen well  theoretically momo yamato the samurai of  wano and those members of the straw hats  and their allies who are still able to  fight could engage the world government  fleet in battle and win but that would  certainly extend this already long arc  even further and it would imply that the  world government sent a pretty  lackluster fleet to take on an enemy who  managed to defeat kaido if i was making  decisions for the world government i  would make sure that this fleet includes  fighters who are extremely strong if not  actual admirals themselves anything  short of that would just be bad planning  so if the fleet is extremely strong and  if the straw hats don't want to just run  away and leave wano to the world  government then it's possible that an  overpowered third party could intervene  to destroy the fleet quickly and move us  along to the next arc for example  zunesha could go beast mode and just  stomp out the entire fleet or the  revolutionaries could show up and  destroy the fleet or maybe blackbeard  will show up and take down the fleet for  some strange reason known only to him  but personally my favorite scenario  would be if shanks and the red hair  pirates showed up and took out the world  government fleet  luffy has now definitely proven that he  is a great pirate he literally took down  a yonko so what better time for the  long-awaited reunion between luffy and  shanks  just imagine luffy waking up from his  post-battle coma to see shanks standing  over him i mean we've been waiting for  this reunion for so long that it almost  seems like a mythical event at this  point it feels like the moment when it  finally happens will never come but with  everything that just happened in wano i  really do think that now is the perfect  time for shanks to reunite with luffy  shanks would then be able to reveal what  he knew and didn't know about the nika  devil fruit why he had a secret meeting  with the gorosei and what kaido's defeat  really means for the balance of power in  the world of one piece  shanks could also usher in the new major  arc in the story by telling luffy and  the others that they have to stop  blackbeard from taking over elbaf or  something along those lines and bam we  have the straw hat pirates and the red  hair pirates sailing together to the  legendary island of elbaf and don't even  get me started on how much meeting  shanks and his crew and then going to  elbaf would affect our boy usopp his  character development would finally  reach its ultimate climax like i said  shanks showing up in this moment is my  personal favorite scenario and i think  that it would make a lot of sense from a  narrative perspective but we'll have to  wait and see we've waited so long for  the epic reunion between luffy and  shanks that any scenario in which it  actually happens seems too good to be  true but speaking of elbaf many fans  believe that this will be the next major  arc in the story after all the loose  sands and guano are wrapped up so what  can we expect from a potential elbaf arc  the island of elbaf is famously  inhabited by giants and its culture and  architecture are inspired by the vikings  elbaf is sometimes referred to as the  strongest country in the world because  of the incredible strength of its giant  army and all the inhabitants of albath  live by a warrior's code of honor for  example if there's an argument or  dispute between giants and neither one  will yield they resolve it through a  battle to the death they believe that  the gods of elbaf will protect the one  who is in the right and so the righteous  one will win and the other one will lose  we first learned about this from dory  and brogi all the way back in chapter  116 usopp was so impressed by the  strength and bravery of the two giants  that he instantly came to think of them  as the exemplars for what a real man and  real warrior should be and usopp  expressed a strong desire to one day  visit elbaf over 900 chapters later the  moment to visit elbaf may finally be at  hand our knowledge of elbaf is quite  limited but we do have some key bits of  information albaf is located in the new  world in a region called warland which  is known for its extremely dangerous  waters and gigantic flora and fauna the  island appears to have large and steep  mountains and there seems to be a  gigantic tree at the center of the  island which is a reference to igdrassil  or the world tree from norse mythology  we also know that elbaf has a prince  named loki and this prince wanted to  marry big mom's daughter lola elbaf was  of course the location of big mom's  former orphanage and big mom aka linlin  is hated by giants all over the world  because of the rampage that she caused  on elbaf as a child big mom was actually  hoping that a marriage between prince  loki and lola would improve her  relationship with the giants but after  lola rejected the marriage and ran away  things got even worse between the giants  and the big mom pirates notably the  religion and culture of elbaf is heavily  centered around the sun and showing  gratitude to the sun and they appear to  worship a son god this means that  luffy's devil fruit the sun god nika  fruit may have a direct connection to  elbaf this is just one of many reasons  why fans believe that elbaf will be the  next major destination for the straw  hats and i tend to agree the only  question is how exactly elbaf will be  tied into the overall story and how it  might incorporate major characters like  dragon shanks and blackbeard at the  stage that the one piece story is at  right now i don't think we will see  another major arc that doesn't directly  involve the big unresolved plot points  in some way and i think that we can all  agree that the 